Decisions 126, 194 (per emit): a C++ embedded emit writes a list of define records with its fingerprint, which a define record has none of, so it is E8012 there, even though the package's baked go emit, which does not select it, never judges it.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// The kinds.
let kinds: [Define] keyed by value = [{ value: 3 }]

/// A count.
let count: Int = 3

emit cpp { out: "@features/ac", namespace: "a", mode: embedded, values: [kinds] }
emit go { out: "@features/a", package: "a", values: [count] }
-- findings.txt --
error[E8012]  a/a.canon:4:5
  kinds cannot be emitted: a load.defines table or record has no representation in generated code

1 error, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
